---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { webAnalyticsEnabled as vercelWebAnalyticsFlag } from '../../lib/web-analytics.mjs';
import { accountSyncV2Enabled as isAccountSyncV2Enabled } from '../../lib/account-v2/feature-flags';
import { weeklyDigestSignupEnabled } from '../../lib/weekly-digest/feature-flags';
import { configuredWalletChains } from '../../lib/wallet/config';

const accountSyncV2Enabled = isAccountSyncV2Enabled({
  PUBLIC_ACCOUNT_SYNC_V2_ENABLED: process.env.PUBLIC_ACCOUNT_SYNC_V2_ENABLED,
  PUBLIC_ACCOUNT_SYNC_V2_PREVIEW_ACK: process.env.PUBLIC_ACCOUNT_SYNC_V2_PREVIEW_ACK,
});
const weeklyDigestEnabled = weeklyDigestSignupEnabled();
const webPushEnabled = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_WEB_PUSH_ENABLED === '1';
const walletChartEnabled = configuredWalletChains({
  ...process.env,
  PUBLIC_WALLET_CHART_ENABLED:
    import.meta.env.PUBLIC_WALLET_CHART_ENABLED ?? process.env.PUBLIC_WALLET_CHART_ENABLED,
}).length > 0;
const updated = '1 October 2026';
const modifiedAt = '2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Privacy at Zodiacs.org',
    url: 'https://zodiacs.org/privacy/',
    description:
      'How Zodiacs.org handles birth charts, browser storage, accounts, share links, Guide, analytics, public wallet lookups, and market-data requests.',
    dateModified: modifiedAt,
  },
];
const webAnalyticsEnabled = vercelWebAnalyticsFlag(import.meta.env);
---
<Base
  title="Privacy — How Your Data Is Handled | Zodiacs.org"
  description="How Zodiacs.org handles birth charts, browser storage, accounts, share links, Guide, analytics, public wallet lookups, and market-data requests."
  path="/privacy/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="section container container--narrow">
    <em class="kicker">Privacy</em>
    <h1 class="method-title display">Your birth details leave your device only when you send them.</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        Chart calculation runs in your browser. Birth fields
        are not sent as part of calculation or a Cabinet of Twelve lookup; they
        leave your device only if you sign in to sync saved charts, share a link
        that carries them, or type them into an assistant message. A transit
        calendar or a compatibility invitation sends chart positions instead,
        and those positions still give your birth date and time. If you
        explicitly attach a chart to the assistant,
        a placements-only summary also leaves the device; saved names and raw
        birth fields are not attached, though its positions still give your
        birth date and time. Aura sends one public wallet address—not your birth or chart
        data—to a blockchain-data provider for a read-only lookup. Accounts{weeklyDigestEnabled ? ',' : ' and'}
        remembered Aura data{weeklyDigestEnabled ? ', and the weekly email' : ''} are optional and off by
        default. We show no ads and use no cross-site tracking.
      </p>

      <h2 id="ai-integrations">AI integration candidates</h2>
      <p>The public-sky ChatGPT candidate needs no birth information or account. When enabled, its tool arguments and results pass through the assistant provider and calculations run on Zodiacs infrastructure. The adapter saves no requests or results, writes no argument logs, uses uncacheable responses and refuses personal fields. Hosting and provider request metadata have separate retention policies; those policies require review before activation. The candidate is disabled by default and has not been publicly submitted.</p>
      <p>The developer plugin computes locally over stdio and makes no outbound requests. An assistant connected to it can still send its tool arguments and results to its provider. Natal positions and exported records can reveal a birth instant; they are not anonymous. Keep them out of public links, analytics, screenshots and issues. The hosted candidate does not offer personal-chart computation or storage.</p>

      <h2>Who operates this site</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Zodiacs LLC</strong>, a New Mexico limited liability company
        (“Zodiacs,” “we,” “us,” or “our”), owns and operates Zodiacs.org and is
        responsible for the personal information described in this policy.
        Where data-protection law uses the term “controller,” Zodiacs LLC is the
        controller for that information.
      </p>

      <h2>What happens when you use a calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Every chart you calculate here is computed on your own device. When you
        enter a birth date, time, and place, that information is used by code
        running in your browser to calculate the chart. It is not transmitted to
        our servers, logged, or stored by us as part of that calculation. It
        leaves the device only if you later sign in to sync a saved chart, share
        a link that carries it, or put it in an assistant message. This is a
        deliberate design choice, described in
        full on our <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Place search downloads from zodiacs.org a city file chosen by the first
        letter you type, and searches it in your browser. For a birth before
        1970, the calculator also downloads a file of historical clock changes
        chosen by the birthplace's time zone. Neither request goes to any other
        service. Which files are requested shows our host the first letter of
        the city you typed and, for a birth before 1970, a group of time zones
        that includes the birthplace's. When a page shows the signs of a birth
        chart, it first requests the pictures of all twelve signs, in the same
        order for every chart, so those requests do not show which signs the
        chart has.
      </p>

      <h2>Guide</h2>
      <p>
        When you send a question to Guide, that message, recent Guide messages,
        and the visible Guide context are sent to OpenAI for an input safety
        check and to generate a draft reply. That generated draft reply is then
        sent back to OpenAI for a second safety check before you see it.
        Every Responses API request uses <code>store: false</code>. The current web Guide conversation stays only
        in this browser session, is not synced to an account, and is not stored
        as text on Zodiacs.org servers, whether or not you are signed in.
        OpenAI states that API data is not used to train its models by default,
        and that its abuse-monitoring logs keep submitted content for up to 30
        days, or longer where the law requires it or where that is needed to
        protect its services or others from harm. Guide offers to attach a
        chart only in the encrypted sync preview, which is off on the public
        site, and only the one chart you marked there as your own. It is
        included only after you press “Attach my chart”; the consent screen
        shows the placements-only summary before it is sent. That summary
        accompanies each question while “Using my chart” remains on; you can
        turn it off. Guide never attaches your saved name, birth date, time,
        birthplace, or coordinates, but the summary's planet positions still
        give your birth date and time, and its ascendant and midheaven, kept
        to the whole degree, give your birthplace roughly. For a chart without
        a birth time, the summary is the sky at 12:00 UTC on the birth date,
        without the Moon, which gives the date but nothing about the
        birthplace. Anything you type into chat is part of the message you
        send.
        To enforce the daily limit, we keep a salted one-way identifier derived
        from your IP address, never the raw IP, with its daily count and a
        record of each request. Each later quota check deletes counts older than
        the previous UTC day and request records older than 48 hours. We do not send
        that identifier to OpenAI or put conversation text in provider metadata.
        Guide also sets a session cookie holding a random, signed identifier. It
        is used to limit simultaneous requests from one browser, lasts until the
        browser session ends, and is not stored with your messages.
      </p>

      <h2>Charts you save</h2>
      <p>
        When you save a chart, it is stored in your browser's local storage —
        on your device, under your control. It is not sent anywhere unless you
        sign in to an account (below), share it or subscribe to its transit
        calendar (below), or attach it to Guide (above).
        Clearing your browser's site data removes saved charts. Unless you sign
        in, we cannot see them and cannot recover them for you.
      </p>

      <h2>Share links and invitations</h2>
      <p>
        Share links keep chart data after the “#” in the address, which browsers
        do not send to servers. A full-details link carries the chart's name,
        birth date, time, place, and coordinates. A positions-only link carries
        the chart code described under “Daily brief, calendar, and
        notifications” instead. Anyone who has either link can open it,
        including anyone it is forwarded to. A link with a preview image also
        puts the Sun, Moon, and rising sign, to the degree, in the address, so
        our server and any app that shows the preview receive them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every image you can make of a chart, a pair of charts or a return — the
        chart sheet and chart cards, the images of a reading, an aspect pattern
        or an explorer section, the compatibility and composite pictures, and
        the solar and lunar return images — is drawn on your device and goes
        only where you share or save it. Unless you choose to show birth details
        on the chart sheet, none has a birth date, time, place, or coordinates,
        and none has a name except a compatibility picture, which shows the
        names of the two charts; none shows more of a birth than its
        positions-only link does. A chart's planet positions are those at the
        birth time in UTC rounded to the whole minute, which still give the
        birth date and time to the minute; the ascendant and midheaven are shown
        only to the whole degree, and Placidus houses are left out. A return
        image is found from those positions and gives the return to the whole
        minute, as does its calendar file. A chart without a birth time is drawn
        from the sky at 12:00 UTC on the birth date, as its link is, which gives
        the date but nothing about the birthplace; the Moon's sign is shown only
        when the Moon stayed in it all that day everywhere, and a picture of two
        charts leaves such a person's Moon out. Each image alone narrows a
        birthplace no more than a link does, but images shared together narrow
        it further. For a birth in Lyon in 1987, a link alone leaves an area of
        about 19,100 km²; a link and one solar return image cast at the
        birthplace, as return images are by default, leave about 3,900 km²,
        about five times smaller; a link with two solar return images and four
        lunar return images leaves about 1,500 km².
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are signed in and create a compatibility invitation from a
        synced chart, our server stores the chart's name (up to 24 characters),
        its Sun sign, its positions-only chart code, and whether the birth time
        is known. An invitation lasts up to 14 days, and whoever opens it sees
        that name and those positions. The positions are erased when the
        invitation is used, withdrawn, or expires, and the rest of the record 30
        days after that.
        If you ask, we email you through
        <a href="https://resend.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resend</a>
        when the invitation is completed.
      </p>

      <h2>Your page: your name and chart cards</h2>
      <p>
        The name you choose for your profile page is stored in this browser
        alongside your saved charts; its first letter, on your Sun sign's
        colour, stands in for a picture there and in the site menu. It leaves
        your device only inside a chart card you choose to send (below), and
        clearing your browser's site data removes it.
      </p>
      <p>
        A chart card is a link you create from the chart marked as yours. It
        carries the name you chose and the chart code described under “Daily
        brief, calendar, and notifications”, so its planet positions still
        give your birth date and time. The card travels in the part of the
        link after the <code>#</code>, which browsers do not send to our
        servers. Anyone who has the link can open it, including anyone it is
        forwarded to. When someone opens it, their browser reads it and
        removes it from the address bar; it is kept on their device only if
        they choose to add it, and we keep no copy.
      </p>

      <h2>Living Chart moments</h2>
      <p>
        Living Chart lets you save an optional category or short note beside a
        dated copy of the personal forecast and factual sky receipt you saw.
        A first save stays in this browser. If you separately choose
        <strong> Keep this on every device</strong>, the entry's date and time
        precision, category, note, frozen forecast, and chart identifier are
        sent to Supabase and stored for your signed-in account. Account access
        is restricted with row-level security and Supabase encrypts stored data
        at rest. This is not end-to-end encryption: Zodiacs.org and Supabase can
        technically process the stored entry to provide synchronization,
        support, export, and deletion.
      </p>
      <p>
        Living Chart sync has its own consent, separate from saved-chart sync.
        We do not make entries public, index them, send them to Guide or another
        AI provider automatically, use them to generate horoscopes, sell them,
        or intentionally include their text in analytics or application logs. Withdrawing
        Living Chart sync deletes the remote entries and advances a consent
        version so an old offline tab cannot upload them again. Copies already
        kept on a device remain until you delete them there or clear this site's
        browser data. Deleting an entry removes its note, category, forecast,
        chart identifier, and date from the device and cloud record. A
        content-free technical deletion marker may remain so a delayed request
        cannot restore it. The timeline provides portable JSON and readable
        Markdown export, per-entry edit and deletion, and a retry control when
        sync needs attention.
      </p>

      <h2>The Cabinet of Twelve and public wallet addresses</h2>
      <p>
        The Cabinet of Twelve reads one public wallet address and the dated sky side by
        side. If you choose to add a chart already saved in this browser, its
        summary is an optional on-device comparison layer. The pattern and any
        symbolic reflection are composed on your device. When you compose or
        refresh an Aura, our holdings endpoint receives the public address and
        forwards it to the configured blockchain-data provider to check which
        Zodiacs.org Registry entries are present. The configured provider is
        currently PublicNode, operated by Allnodes. The provider receives the
        lookup from our server, not from your browser. The request does not
        include birth fields, chart names, chart placements, or chart geometry.
        When the feature is enabled, Zodiac Terminal's optional
        public Shelf uses the same endpoint and sends one public Solana address,
        the one you enter, only after you press View; it does not send chart or
        birth data. When Aura is off, the illustrative Shelf makes no address
        or provider request.
      </p>
      {walletChartEnabled && (
        <p>
          The Wallet Chart page sends the public address you paste to our
          server, which asks a blockchain-data provider (a Solana RPC service,
          Etherscan, or a Base RPC service) for the address's first transaction
          and the Registry signs it holds, and keeps the answer in memory for up
          to a day. No birth or chart data is sent.
        </p>
      )}
      <p>
        You can paste a public address without connecting a wallet. If you
        choose Connect, compatible third-party wallet software is invoked only
        after your click. It may return the public accounts you authorize to
        this browser; Aura selects one compatible address and forwards only that
        address for the lookup. Aura does not request a recovery phrase, private
        key, message signature, token approval, transaction, or network switch.
        Your wallet provider's own privacy terms apply to its software and
        connection prompt.
      </p>
      <p>
        A public address is public but not necessarily anonymous. Its on-chain
        holdings and history may be visible and may become linked with a person
        or other activity. Vercel, the configured blockchain-data provider, and
        their infrastructure may process routine request metadata and
        operational or security logs, such as IP address, time, and browser
        information. We do not promise that a public-address request is never
        logged by infrastructure providers whose retention practices we do not
        control.
      </p>

      <h2>Public Astrofolio, Terminal, and Registry data sources</h2>
      <p>
        When a relevant Zodiac Terminal or Registry market panel is displayed, your browser may request
        public market data from Dex Screener, public chart data from GeckoTerminal,
        or public attention data from Wikimedia, and opening a Terminal market asks
        independent Jupiter for a price quote on a sample amount. Those automatic requests do not include a wallet address,
        birth fields, chart data, or Aura results. The independent service still
        receives ordinary web-request metadata, such as your IP address,
        browser information, and request time, and its own privacy terms and
        retention practices apply.
      </p>
      <p>
        On the Astrofolio How to Buy page, opening the page or changing the selected sign does not load
        Jupiter, contact wallet software, or request a quote. After you explicitly load the optional
        convenience tool, your browser sends the selected token mint and requested amount as quote parameters
        to independent Jupiter and requests indexed-liquidity context from Dex Screener. Those display requests
        do not include a wallet address. If you choose to review a direct swap, the compatible wallet you select
        supplies its public Solana address to Jupiter so Jupiter can build the exact transaction for your review.
        Your wallet signs locally. Your browser then sends the signed transaction and Jupiter request identifier
        to Jupiter's execution endpoint. Neither the public address nor the signed transaction is sent to a
        Zodiacs.org server, and Zodiacs.org never asks for or receives a recovery phrase or private key. Jupiter,
        Dex Screener, and your wallet service may receive ordinary web-request metadata such as your IP address,
        browser information, and request time; their own privacy terms and retention practices apply.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each sign&rsquo;s Registry profile is read-only. It shows public market data
        and verified token addresses, but it contains no purchase route or link
        to a trading venue. The profile does not connect a wallet, request a
        quote, receive your public address, or ask for a transaction. No birth
        or chart data is included in these market-data requests.
      </p>

      <h2>Aura browser storage and sharing</h2>
      <p>
        By default, Aura keeps the public address, chain, Registry sign results,
        lookup time, and optional selected chart identifier in this tab's session
        storage. It becomes ineligible for restoration after eight hours. The
        unchecked “Remember this address on this device” option stores the same
        fields in local storage and makes them ineligible after 24 hours.
        Ineligible records are deleted the next time Aura reads them; if you do
        not return, the browser may retain the expired bytes until you clear site
        data. “Forget address / Clear Aura data” removes both Aura records from
        this browser; it cannot erase public blockchain history or
        infrastructure logs.
      </p>
      <p>
        Aura share images are composed on your device. The image omits the
        public address, chart name, birth fields, exact placements, and chart
        geometry. The seal image shows which signs are held, how many of the
        twelve, and a date. The cabinet image shows the chain, the date, which
        signs are held, and each one's edition, which reflects the balance, with
        a count of gold sculptures up to 99+. Neither includes a saved-chart
        fact. A browser share sheet or download sends the image to
        a destination you choose, whose
        privacy terms then apply. Clearing Aura cannot recall copies that other
        people or services have saved or reposted.
      </p>

      <h2>Optional account (sync across devices)</h2>
      {accountSyncV2Enabled ? (
        <>
          <p>
            Accounts remain optional. Account-free calculators and local chart
            saving work without signing in. The encrypted sync canary accepts at
            most one chart that you explicitly confirm is your own. The preview
            is limited to adults aged 18 or older.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              You sign in with a one-time link sent to your email address. A
              first-party session token remains in this browser until sign-out.
            </li>
            <li>
              Before upload, the profile page shows the exact birth source and
              derived placement data that would leave the device. No chart is
              selected or migrated automatically.
            </li>
            <li>
              The saved label, exact date, time, place, coordinates, timezone,
              and derived placements are encrypted by our server with a
              per-record data key. That key is wrapped by a service key stored
              outside the database. This is service-managed encryption—not
              end-to-end encryption—so Zodiacs can decrypt the record when you
              restore it on another signed-in device.
            </li>
            <li>
              The database receives an encrypted chart envelope plus minimal
              identifiers, revisions, consent state, and deletion authority
              needed for synchronization. The chart is not public, used for
              discovery, sent to an AI provider, or licensed for advertising by
              this consent.
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://supabase.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Supabase</a>{' '}
              processes account and database records, and{' '}
              <a href="https://vercel.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel</a>{' '}
              runs the server boundary that validates and encrypts them.
            </li>
            <li>
              To make deletion reliable after an account email changes, we keep
              a bounded history of up to 16 confirmed account-email locators.
              Each locator is encrypted with a service-managed key; the database
              does not receive the plaintext address. During deletion, a
              request-bound encrypted cleanup record may remain for up to seven
              days while removal from the email provider is retried. It is used
              only for that cleanup and is then deleted with the recovery receipt.
            </li>
            <li>
              Withdrawing chart-sync consent immediately erases the v2 remote
              encrypted chart record. Local copies stay on devices
              unless you separately clear them.
            </li>
            <li>
              You can download a JSON account export or initiate permanent
              deletion from the profile page. Account deletion also removes a
              linked, independently confirmed Daily Sun subscription when that
              cleanup can be confirmed. If an email change or key rotation makes
              the match ambiguous, account erasure still completes and the page
              tells you to use the email’s unsubscribe link or contact support.
            </li>
            <li>
              Accounts with charts from the earlier cloud-sync system are not
              silently migrated. The canary pauses and offers export until an
              explicit chart-by-chart migration review is available; permanent
              account deletion removes those legacy records too.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <p>
            You can create a free account to keep your saved charts on more than one
            device. This is entirely optional and the tools work fully without it.
            If you create one:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              You sign in with a one-time link sent to your email address — there is
              no password to store.
            </li>
            <li>
              We store your email address and every chart saved in your browser
              while you are signed in, including those saved before you signed
              in, with their birth details, with our database
              provider, <a href="https://supabase.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Supabase</a>,
              so they can appear on your other devices. Access is restricted to your
              own account.
            </li>
            <li>
              We also store your house-system setting and a record of each chart
              you delete (its identifier and when), so the deletion reaches your
              other devices. These are kept until you delete the account.
            </li>
            <li>
              While you are signed in, a sign-in token is kept in your browser so
              you stay logged in. Signing out removes it.
            </li>
            <li>
              You can delete your account and its stored charts at any time by
              emailing <a href="mailto:admin@zodiacs.org">admin@zodiacs.org</a>.
              Copies in our weekly backups expire within 90 days (see Backups).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </>
      )}

      <h2>Email</h2>
      {weeklyDigestEnabled && (
        <p>
          Account holders can opt in to a weekly email summarizing the coming
          week's sky for their saved charts. It is unchecked by default. If you
          opt in, we store that preference and send the email through our email
          provider, <a href="https://resend.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resend</a>.
          Every email includes a one-click unsubscribe link, and you can turn it
          off from your profile at any time.
        </p>
      )}
      <p>
        Your account email address is used to send sign-in links and, if you ask
        for it, a note when someone completes a compatibility invitation you
        sent. We do not sell or share it.
      </p>

      <h2>Daily brief, calendar, and notifications</h2>
      <p>
        The daily brief reads computed positions from a chart saved on your
        device.
      </p>
      <p>
        A transit calendar feed carries a positions-only chart code in its web
        address. Our server, its cache, and your calendar service receive that
        code each time the calendar refreshes. The code has no name, date, time,
        or place fields. Its planet positions still give your birth date and
        time to the minute: they are taken at the birth time in UTC rounded to
        the whole minute. The ascendant and midheaven are rounded to the degree,
        which still narrows the birthplace to an area about one degree of
        longitude wide: about 110 km at the equator, 80 km at 45° north or
        south, and 55 km at 60°. From north to south the area is at least 400 km
        within 15° of the equator, 200 km within 45°, and 70 km within 60°;
        further north it can be narrower, and near the Arctic Circle it can be a
        strip less than a kilometre from north to south. A chart without a birth
        time has no ascendant or midheaven, and its code carries the sky at
        12:00 UTC on the birth date, which gives the date but nothing about the
        birthplace. Codes made by an earlier version of the site can carry more.
        For a chart without a birth time they carry noon at the birthplace,
        which gives its time zone or, before standard time, its longitude, and a
        picture of two charts made with such a code draws that chart from those
        positions, not from the sky at 12:00 UTC. For a birth before standard
        time, when a chart keeps the birthplace's own mean time, they carry the
        second of the birth, which narrows the birthplace to a few strips about
        3 km wide or less. Calendar addresses made before 23 September 2026 also
        carry the ascendant and midheaven more precisely; our server now rounds
        them before use. A calendar address never changes by itself, so to
        replace one made by an earlier version, such as one for a chart without
        a birth time or for a birth before standard time, remove that calendar
        and subscribe again.
      </p>
      <p>
        A calendar file you download from the Transits page is built in your
        browser from your chart as calculated there, not from the chart code,
        and its times are exact. Anyone you share it with, or any online
        calendar you import it into, can work out from them your birth date and
        time, and your birthplace from those for your ascendant or midheaven;
        without a birth time the chart is calculated for noon at your
        birthplace, so they give its time zone or, before standard time, its
        longitude.
      </p>
      {webPushEnabled && (
        <p>
          If you turn on daily notifications, we store your browser's push
          subscription — a vendor push-service URL and its delivery keys — with
          your language setting and no birth data, so we can send the note. You
          can turn notifications off at any time.
        </p>
      )}

      <h2>Public People pages</h2>
      <p>
        The People directory uses names, public birth dates and places, life
        dates, disciplines, and licensed portraits from reviewed Wikidata,
        Wikipedia, and Wikimedia Commons records. The chart is computed from
        those sourced facts and describes the recorded sky and its uncertainty;
        it does not make claims about a person's health, conduct, relationships,
        finances, or private life. Profiles of living people are not submitted
        to search engines. To request a correction, withholding, or removal,
        email <a href="mailto:people@zodiacs.org">people@zodiacs.org</a>.
        We honor a subject's removal request even when the underlying public
        source remains unchanged.
      </p>

      <h2>The Race</h2>
      <p>
        If you join a team in the Race, we store a one-way code derived from the
        Race cookie, with your team, the season, when you joined, and your
        weekly check-ins. To limit repeat joins we also keep a one-way code
        derived from your IP address, which is deleted after the next UTC day.
        No name, email address, account, or wallet is involved.
      </p>

      <h2>Backups</h2>
      <p>
        Once a week we copy the database, which holds accounts, synced charts,
        and the other stored records this page describes. The copy is encrypted
        with AES-256 before it is stored with GitHub, and each copy is deleted
        after 90 days. Deleting your account removes it from the live database;
        it can remain in a backup until that backup expires.
      </p>

      <h2 id="compute-api">The compute API</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/developers/compute/">compute API</a> is for programs: it
        computes a chart, positions, houses, events, a local time or a sky
        fact from what a program sends it. The site's own calculators do not
        use it. It reads the body of each request, which can hold a birth
        date, time and place, and nothing from the query string. Nothing from
        a request or its result is written to a log, a file or a database, no
        error repeats what was sent, and every response is marked so that no
        cache stores it. While an instance of the API is running, it keeps in
        memory the public time zone and ephemeris tables it has loaded to
        answer, which show which time zones and periods have been asked
        about. The ephemeris library it uses also keeps two values from its
        last calculations, to reuse them: sidereal time at the moment of the
        last chart or houses request, and the Earth's tilt at the last moment
        any calculation used. So those two moments stay in that instance's
        memory until later requests replace them or the instance stops; no
        place is kept. To enforce the rate limit, the API sends the request's headers,
        which include your IP address, to Vercel's firewall, which counts the
        requests from each address; it never sends the body. Our host's logs,
        described below, keep the full web address of each request, so birth
        details belong in the body, not in the address.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting, logs, and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on <a href="https://vercel.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel</a>.
        Like all web hosts, their servers process the requests your browser
        makes and may keep short-lived technical logs (such as IP address and
        browser type) to deliver the site and guard against abuse. Those logs
        keep the full web address of each request, which for a transit
        calendar includes its chart code and for a link with a preview image
        includes the Sun, Moon, and rising sign. We do not run
        advertising, and we use no cross-site tracking cookies or third-party
        marketing pixels.
      </p>
      {accountSyncV2Enabled ? (
        <p>
          Third-party analytics are disabled throughout the access-controlled
          encrypted-sync preview. This prevents an analytics script from
          sharing the same page context as private browser chart storage.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          We count page views and anonymous feature usage with Plausible, a
          cookieless analytics service. To avoid counting the same device
          repeatedly during one day, Plausible briefly processes the IP address
          and user agent to derive an identifier scoped to this site, device,
          and day. The raw IP and user agent are not stored; the salt used for
          that identifier rotates and is deleted every 24 hours. Plausible
          receives no birth data, public address, chart identifier, connected
          account identifier, or exact held-sign list. It also receives no
          cross-site identifier.
          Aura events carry only allowlisted categories such as an outcome and
          a coarse held-count bucket; other events similarly record “a chart was
          saved,” never whose.
        </p>
      )}
      {webAnalyticsEnabled && !accountSyncV2Enabled && (
        <p>
          We also count page views with Vercel Web Analytics, the cookieless
          counter built into our hosting platform. It records the page path
          only (query strings and fragments are removed before anything is
          sent), tells devices apart within one day using a hash derived from
          the request that is discarded after that day, and receives none of
          the event data described above.
        </p>
      )}

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We do not use advertising or tracking cookies. Three first-party cookies
        are sent to our server by design: Guide's session cookie, until the
        browser session ends; the Race's cookie, for up to a year; and an
        invitation cookie, for up to 14 days while you use a compatibility
        invitation. The rest is first-party browser storage for features you
        use: what you save (charts, comparisons, Living Chart moments, learning
        progress), working state for the tools you use (such as Guide's
        conversation and cached calculations), bounded Aura session data, an
        optional remembered Aura address, site preferences, copies of the site's
        own files for offline use, and, if you sign in, a sign-in token. Apart
        from these cookies and what the sections above describe, this storage
        stays on your device, and none of it is used to track you across other
        sites.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The site is intended for a general audience and is not directed at
        children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
        them.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use every calculator with no account; nothing you enter is stored off your device unless you sign in, share a chart, or subscribe to its calendar.</li>
        <li>Use the Aura example without a chart, address, wallet connection, or purchase.</li>
        <li>Paste a public address instead of connecting third-party wallet software.</li>
        <li>Leave Aura's “Remember” option unchecked and clear its browser data at any time.</li>
        <li>Delete saved charts by clearing your browser's data for this site.</li>
        {accountSyncV2Enabled
          ? <li>Export or delete an account from the profile page; choose separately whether to clear this browser.</li>
          : <li>Delete an account and its synced data by emailing us.</li>}
        {weeklyDigestEnabled && <li>Turn the weekly email off with one click, any time.</li>}
        <li>Withdraw a compatibility invitation from your profile before it is used.</li>
        <li>Request correction, withholding, or removal of a People profile.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change how we handle data, we will update this page and its date.
        Material changes to the account or email features will be reflected here
        before they take effect.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy and deletion requests may be sent to Zodiacs LLC at{' '}
        <a href="mailto:admin@zodiacs.org">admin@zodiacs.org</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="method-updated mono">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
